From 1b51fab761fb4b6c5cc44ab903b03801ecb2a110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Michaud <jmichaud@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:52:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] [mya] Look up symbols by name on Linux Need the bug URL
 (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Snapshot::symbol() reported "not supported" on Linux. It now searches each
image of the snapshot, in the loader's order, through the image's dynamic
section, GNU hash table, dynamic symbol table and version table, as
dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT) does: only exported symbols, at their default version; a
thread-local or an indirect function (whose symbol is its resolver) is not
found. glibc relocates the dynamic section's addresses in place on most
architectures but leaves them as offsets where the section is read-only
(RISC-V), and both are handled. Every table is bounded by new CorpseLimits,
and the whole lookup by the same read budget as on Darwin.

The `mya heap` command added later in this series finds s_recentVM and
g_commonVMOrNull through it.

The diagnostic counter ExportsTriesSearched becomes SymbolTablesSearched,
since it now counts GNU hash tables too. The Symbol suite runs on Linux,
and linuxSkip, which nothing uses any more, is removed.

